## 8. Lessons Learned

1. Always establish whether an issue affects one user or multiple users.
2. Verify mailbox permissions before making configuration changes.
3. Confirm authorisation before granting mailbox access.
4. Use Outlook on the web to help isolate Outlook Desktop issues.
5. Allow time for Exchange Online permission changes to propagate.
6. Distinguish between Full Access and Send As permissions.
7. Verify the complete user experience before resolving an incident.

